  "body": "### What this PR does / why we need it?\r\n\r\nThe HCCL backend duplicated the trainer/worker weight-transfer orchestration already provided by upstream vLLM's NCCL engines. This PR reuses that implementation and retains the HCCL-specific rendezvous, NPU data plane, device binding and communicator lifecycle.\r\n\r\n- Build the worker and trainer engines on `NCCLWeightTransferEngine` and `NCCLTrainerWeightTransferEngine`. Reuse the upstream layerwise-reload lifecycle, trainer send orchestration, metadata/iterator checks and worker initialization payload.\r\n- Define `HCCLWeightTransferInitInfo` in `hccl_common.py` as a subclass of upstream `NCCLWeightTransferInitInfo`. Reuse upstream rank fields and rendezvous validation while retaining HCCL's required TCP endpoint and optional packed settings; reject NCCL-only unique-ID rendezvous.\r\n- Register `HCCLTrainerInitInfo` and `HCCLTrainerWeightTransferEngine` with `WeightTransferTrainerFactory`. Align the trainer's default with upstream: `packed=True`.\r\n- Keep HCCL-specific endpoint creation and explicitly assign trainer rank 0 and worker rank offset 1.\r\n- Synchronize inherited packed settings during initialization and re-initialization. Preserve optional per-update packed settings and reject conflicts with values fixed at initialization.\r\n- Bind transfers to the assigned NPU and normalize source tensors before broadcasting. In unpacked mode, synchronize each broadcast to keep its staging tensor alive until the collective completes.\r\n- Explicitly close HCCL communicators on shutdown and initialization/send failures. Reject further sends from failed or closed trainers.\r\n- Remove the legacy worker-side static `trainer_init`, `trainer_send_weights` and `HCCLTrainerSendWeightsArgs`, without forwarding wrappers.\r\n- Migrate both RL examples and the HCCL state-transition E2E test to the trainer factory, upstream HTTP/Ray weight-sync clients and `engine.send_weights()`.\r\n\r\nThe PR changes seven files: the HCCL engine, HCCL common helpers, backend registration, HCCL unit tests, two RL examples and the HCCL state-transition E2E test.\r\n\r\nThe packed utility fixes remain in #19127. This PR does not modify `packed_tensor.py` or `npu_ipc_engine.py`, and the existing packed skip in the checked-in E2E test remains unchanged.\r\n\r\n### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?\r\n\r\nYes. Trainer integrations using the removed static interfaces must migrate to `WeightTransferTrainerFactory`, `HCCLTrainerInitInfo`, a weight source and an upstream weight-sync client. The updated HTTP and Ray examples demonstrate the new API.\r\n\r\nThe new trainer defaults to `packed=True`, matching upstream. Set `packed=False` explicitly to use unpacked transfers.\r\n\r\nThe `hccl` backend name and optional per-update packed settings remain supported. Conflicting initialization and update settings now raise an explicit `ValueError`. No new environment variable or CLI flag is introduced.\r\n\r\n### How was this patch tested?\r\n\r\n**Unit tests — without #19127**\r\n\r\n- **178 passed** across `tests/ut/distributed/weight_transfer` and `tests/ut/distributed/device_communicators`.\r\n- A separate rerun of `tests/ut/distributed/weight_transfer/test_hccl_engine.py` completed with **32 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped**.\r\n- Coverage includes upstream inheritance and orchestration, packed defaults, initialization/re-initialization, sender/non-sender handshakes, worker rank offset, packed-setting conflicts, source normalization, device binding, both receive modes, shutdown and failure guards. Additional coverage checks the inherited init-info payload round trip, required TCP rendezvous and invalid packed initialization settings.\r\n\r\n**Real-NPU E2E — with #19127**\r\n\r\nValidated the working-tree changes subsequently committed as `ee8cb3650`, together with `packed_tensor.py` and `npu_ipc_engine.py` from #19127. Those fixes were applied only to the validation snapshot and are not included in this PR.\r\n\r\nThe test used the full Qwen3-30B-A3B checkpoint: **18,867 tensors, 56.87 GiB**, inference **TP=2**, and a separate trainer NPU, giving HCCL world size 3.\r\n\r\nThe trainer factory and upstream `HTTPVLLMWeightSyncClient` drove two complete updates in each transfer mode. Every round broadcast the entire checkpoint.\r\n\r\n| Mode | Round | Transfer time | Generated text/tokens | Maximum logprob error |\r\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n| Packed | 1 | 39.13 s | Exact match | 0.0 |\r\n| Packed | 2 | 42.29 s | Exact match | 0.0 |\r\n| Unpacked | 1 | 107.90 s | Exact match | 0.0 |\r\n| Unpacked | 2 | 107.50 s | Exact match | 0.0 |\r\n\r\nFour fixed prompts covered English, Chinese and code generation. All rounds matched the pre-transfer baseline exactly. Transfer times are functional-test observations, not performance benchmarks.\r\n\r\n**RL examples — rerun at `ee8cb3650` with the same #19127 overlay**\r\n\r\nBoth examples were rerun successfully against the latest commit after the init-info relocation. The example files and their original validation assertions were unchanged. The 4,542-file validation snapshot was checksum-verified before and after execution.\r\n\r\n- `rlhf_http_hccl.py`: Qwen3-0.6B completed the weight update and all four post-update generations; exit code 0.\r\n- `rlhf_async_new_apis.py`: Qwen3-1.7B-Base → Qwen3-1.7B completed pause, transfer, resume and fresh-model comparison. **13/13 requests passed the original exact token-ID assertions**; exit code 0.\r\n\r\nThe example runs did not add logprob assertions; exact logprob comparison was covered by the full-checkpoint E2E test above.\r\n\r\n**Environment and scope**\r\n\r\nReal-NPU validation used `vllm-ascend:nightly-main-a3-openeuler-1017`, Python 3.12.13, vLLM `0.31.0+empty`, torch `2.10.0+cpu` and torch-npu `2.10.0.post4`. The Ray example validation used Ray 2.48.0. The 4,542-file source snapshot was checksum-verified before and after the latest E2E run.\r\n\r\nMulti-node, DP>1, MTP/draft weight updates and optimizer-step scenarios were not exercised.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Checklist\r\n\r\n#### Testing\r\n\r\n- [x] **Boundary / edge-case coverage:** packed defaults, re-initialization, sender/non-sender initialization and source-device normalization.\r\n- [x] **Regression coverage:** worker rank offset, packed-setting synchronization, upstream send orchestration and failed-trainer retry guards.\r\n- [x] **Error / failure path coverage:** invalid/conflicting settings, failed initialization/send, repeated shutdown and sends after failure or close.\r\n- [x] **Integration validation:** latest real-weight packed/unpacked transfers and reruns of both affected RL examples, with the tested versions and #19127 dependency documented above.\r\n- [ ] **Performance impact:** no performance benchmark attached.\r\n\r\nco-authored with: @Windfeng8\r\n\r\n\n- vLLM main: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c0b6f74bee518aeaf5d72b200a0216e72fbb5e7c\n",
